{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth","id":887484,"title":"Prime Arcanum as Truth","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-10T14:15:56-07:00","id":887484,"title":"Prime Arcanum as Truth","content":"The Prime Arcanum used to be the Arcanum you would take for a couple of interesting spells and that would be it. In the new edition, Prime is back with a vengeance: first off there are so many tthings to do with magic now that Priime is really useful to cope with leylines, embued items, grimoires etc. But I think it's very interesting that Prime Arcanum's perview was changed from illusions to Truth. And I'd like to know what kind of Prime spells you would come up with when you use Prime as a resonant for the Higher Truths and not just weaving magic. In my opinion Prime could had benefited from more examples about how it could be used to manipulate the Truth without competing with the Mind Arcanum.<br /> <br /> So, in a nutshells do you think that Prime could be used to:<br /> <br /> Blind the Sleepers about a spell being cast by Veiling Magic ?<br /> Open Doors by revealing the Truth to someone who won't face it ?<br /> Cure trauma by showing where the real issues are ?<br /> Awaken a sleeper by opening him to the Truth or making the Lie evident to him ?<br /> <br /> What do you think Prime spells dealing with Truth should look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:24:42-07:00","id":887491,"title":"","content":"Words of Truth is a great example of the social-benefit-from-Truth option, and I think between Apocalypse and Stealing Fire (mage sight and Sleepwalker-enating) we're pushing the limits of Awakening; I really don't think making someone Awaken fully should be reliably possible with magic, but Prime's definitely the place to go for opening people's eyes to magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T14:32:04-07:00","id":887499,"title":"","content":"Yes I love them and the concept is so new, I want more ^^<br /> My players were thrilled about Prime being also about the Supernal Truths and it really makes more sense than Prime being about illusions. As a brand new concept I think sharing opinions and ideas about how it could work should be interesting and even enlightening<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:03:23-07:00","id":887527,"title":"","content":"Theoretically a Veiling of Truth ought to be able to cause an illusion though. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T15:03:55-07:00","id":887529,"title":"","content":"Well, lets see, some Truth spells.<br /> <br /> <b>Conceal Gifts (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Science, Subterfuge, Stealth<br /> Withstand: Wits</i><br /> Hiding isn't always easy for the awakened and sometimes, even when they try to be discreet, their consistent runs of &quot;good luck&quot; or excessive skill, the fact that they always seem to know more than they should, those things will add up over time and might breed suspicion in the minds of others. This spell however cloaks the truth of their supernal gifts in such a way that anything the mage does with their magics, so long as it is not outright magical, will appear natural and not arouse suspicion even if it does cross the boundary into the outright strange. If the mage states the cause of death for a corpse after just a momentary glance it will be assumed to be a hunch, or a lie, and the same would go for the extreme luck they demonstrate in a firefight or their seven-in-a-row winning-streak.<br /> Anyone with a power trait is immune to this effect.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> - Those with power traits have to roll a Clash of Wills or they too will fall under the influence of this spell.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> - Not only will the effect apply to things people were around for but also to other things such as rumours, a history of incredible investment success and similar.<br /> <br /> <b>Twist Truth (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Empathy, Persuasion<br /> Withstand: Resolve</i><br /> Convincing people of the truth that you know when they already have their own can be a chore and a challenge because almost no matter what one says they might disregard it, or maybe one can't even discuss it with them. This spell allows the mage to change the truth the subject knows, entirely without speaking to them. Each point of potency allows for one fact to be changed for the duration of the spell, but they can only be changed to the truth that the caster themselves is convinced of, not fabricated entirely, though one can certainly be selective in which bits are changed so as to lead the subject to an entirely different conclusion.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> - The truth will out, or rather the subject will try to spread their newfound truth. At least once per day, for the duration, they will try to convince someone else of their newfound insights.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> - The subject will not take the changes in their beliefs as newfound insight but believe it to be what they thought all along.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b> - Costs 1 mana. The effect are made lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T19:00:17-07:00","id":948253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth?p=887529#post887529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Twist Truth (Prime \u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Practice: Ruling<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Academics, Empathy, Persuasion<br /> Withstand: Resolve</i><br /> Convincing people of the truth that you know when they already have their own can be a chore and a challenge because almost no matter what one says they might disregard it, or maybe one can't even discuss it with them. This spell allows the mage to change the truth the subject knows, entirely without speaking to them. Each point of potency allows for one fact to be changed for the duration of the spell, but they can only be changed to the truth that the caster themselves is convinced of, not fabricated entirely, though one can certainly be selective in which bits are changed so as to lead the subject to an entirely different conclusion.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> - The truth will out, or rather the subject will try to spread their newfound truth. At least once per day, for the duration, they will try to convince someone else of their newfound insights.<br /> <b>+1 Reach</b> - The subject will not take the changes in their beliefs as newfound insight but believe it to be what they thought all along.<br /> <b>+2 Reach</b> - Costs 1 mana. The effect are made lasting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome though this is, it seems much more like a Patterning spell (i.e. wholly transforming Truths), rather than a Ruling spell (i.e. twisting Truths into doing something abnormal/slightly unnatural to them, without actually transforming them or altering their inherent qualities), especially given Words of Truth as a precedent example of a Ruling Prime spell dealing with Truths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11673-corwyn_ulhar","name":"Corwyn_Ulhar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T20:55:54-07:00","id":948328,"title":"","content":"A fair argument and I can certainly see why it would be ruled as such. It was just something I threw together in ten minutes, just to give some examples <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And in retrospect I feel this thread is actually far more interesting than I thought it was at the time. Thread-necromancy anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T00:25:24-07:00","id":948421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MorkaisChosen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth?p=887491#post887491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Words of Truth is a great example of the social-benefit-from-Truth option, and I think between Apocalypse and Stealing Fire (mage sight and Sleepwalker-enating) we're pushing the limits of Awakening; I really don't think making someone Awaken fully should be reliably possible with magic, but Prime's definitely the place to go for opening people's eyes to magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I literally made Legacy based on this new preview - <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/933264-2e-illusionists-of-truth-%E2%80%93-magicians-legacy\">Illusionists of Truth</a></b> - in 1E it was about concealing Truth in mundane stage magicians ( and others performers ) illusions - so it used 'illusions' preview of 1E. Now it can work with proper 'truths' of Prime of 2E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-11-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:25:57-07:00","id":948846,"title":"","content":"With Prime Ruling you could do something along the lines of a parable or parallel story that everyone listening would recognize for its deeper truth. Perhaps Reach would allow selection of traits that make the truth obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T15:00:50-07:00","id":948882,"title":"","content":"<b>Seek Truth</b> (Prime <b>\u2022</b>)<br /> <br /> Practice: Compelling.<br /> Primary Factor: Potency<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Occult, Empathy, Investigation.<br /> Withstand: Resolve<br /> <br /> Even when blinded by the Quiessence, sleepers still hunger for the deeper meaning of Supernal Truths. This dangerous spell nudges those instincts and drives the target to seek out higher meaning<b><i> as they understand it</i></b>. This grants the sleeper the specific Aspiration &quot;look for higher meaning&quot; for the duration of the spell. However it offers no ability for the target to understand how to fulfill that goal. For some this may drive them towards their church, a laboratory or the local bar where they feel they can be themselves. However for those sleepers who have had a brush with the supernatural that they've pushed out of their minds, there's a chance it may direct them back on the path towards it again. While some mages use this spell on witnesses to a mystery that matches their obsessions, this risks provoking dissonance, integrity loss and all the other dangers of pushing sleepers towards the supernatural. In most consillia this spell violates the Lex Magica.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach - The spell can compel a sleepwalker rather than just a sleeper.<br /> +2 Reach - The spell can compel a supernatural being that possesses the integrity trait.<br /> <br /> <b>Note:</b> <i>Granting an aspiration is usually well and truly beyond a compelling spell. However because this goal can't be selected by the caster and doesn't change anything about how the target interprets that goal, this doesn't seem too far against balance IMO.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:08:04-07:00","id":949836,"title":"","content":"<b>Lost Words</b> (Prime <b>\u2022\u2022</b>)<br /> <br /> Practice: Veiling<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Expression, Subterfuge, Stealth.<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> <br /> The High Speech is not a true language, but because of its link to Supernal meaning it can be used to communicate with other Mages. While that true meaning can not be taken away, it can be concealed to the point where it can no longer be perceived and understood. This spell can be used one of two ways. Either it can be used to prevent the target from understanding any high speech that they hear during the duration, or it can be used to conceal any high speech that the target speaks themselves so that others can't understand it. If the target is prevented from understanding high speech then their peripheral mage sight will not register when high speech is spoken. If the target is prevented from communicating in high speech then they will not trigger the peripheral mage sight of others when it is used.<br /> <br /> This does not affect the use of High Speech as a Yantra in a spell which will still provide all normal bonuses. The meaning of the High Speech used in the spell will be still be concealed, however when used as a Yantra even if the High Speech itself is concealed the spell being cast will still register normally to all forms of mage sight.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach - The spell prevents the target from both speaking and understanding High Speech as a language, however it does not affect the use of High Speech as a Yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:08:01-07:00","id":950014,"title":"","content":"Just curious, when using High Speech as a Yantra Sleepers in the area don't understand it anyway but it sounds like glossalia to them. So how does this make High Speech sound to them?<br /> <br /> Also, do you think it would be possible to create a spell of some sort that makes it possible to sort of water down, or change the way High Speech works enough to use it as a more effective means of communication? In other words making it able to communicate more than simple, direct ideas, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 08-13-2016, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T07:30:54-07:00","id":950024,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, we have whole topic on this subject... <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants\">Option - High Speech Variants</a></b><br /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T08:02:25-07:00","id":950033,"title":"","content":"No, we don't. That thread doesn't address my question at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:08:16-07:00","id":950214,"title":"","content":"Oh! How about a Prime Patterning spell that causes a lie to become true?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:21:33-07:00","id":950249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth?p=950214#post950214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! How about a Prime Patterning spell that causes a lie to become true?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spells, including Prime, rely on imposing Supernal Truths onto the Phenomenal world. The Lie isn't by definition a Truth. Therefore it shouldn't be possible to define it with Prime. That you even have the capability to consider this action highlights the highest crime the Exarchs have committed. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Although maybe you could accomplish this with the Parametric language. But beware the Gate.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T15:28:56-07:00","id":950257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth?p=950214#post950214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! How about a Prime Patterning spell that causes a lie to become true?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An interesting idea, and what could possibly go wrong... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:27:47-07:00","id":950354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth?p=950014#post950014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just curious, when using High Speech as a Yantra Sleepers in the area don't understand it anyway but it sounds like glossalia to them. So how does this make High Speech sound to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in physical reality the mage is just speaking glossalia. Even other mages just hear glossalia normally, however their peripheral mage sense activates and they perceive the meaning behind the nonsense sounds. I'd say normally other mages would hear glossalia and it would sound like a Mage trying (but failing somehow) to speak in the High Speech. Since this could give the spell away, maybe there are two additional reaches you could add to the spell.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach: The High Speech just sounds like an ordinary language, the veil makes it sound like something unimportant or just idle chit-chat that listeners won't pay attention to or remember (as per the mind veil in the book, but only for the High Speech itself). <br /> +2 Reach: The High Speech sounds like ordinary language but the caster of the Lost Speech spell can decide what the target appears to be saying in an ordinary language. (It is impossible to make someone appear to say something different in High Speech though, as High Speech cannot contain falsehoods).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/887484-prime-arcanum-as-truth?p=950014#post950014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, do you think it would be possible to create a spell of some sort that makes it possible to sort of water down, or change the way High Speech works enough to use it as a more effective means of communication? In other words making it able to communicate more than simple, direct ideas, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficult since that goes against the nature of it, so I'd say it would be a Patterning effect to transform High Speech into something else. Perhaps:<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle Speech</b> (Prime <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>)<br /> <br /> Practice: Patterning<br /> Primary Factor: Duration<br /> Suggested Rote Skills: Expression, Academics, Occult.<br /> Withstand: Composure<br /> <br /> Those under the influence of this spell are able to speak an alternate version of the High Speech, transformed by this spell. The sounds they produce become more complex and through the spell they can weave in elaborate symbols into the meaning that the High Speech conveys to any listening Mage. Alternatively more complex written High Speech can also be produced (and remains once the duration elapses). This form of High Speech can convey complex ideas to anyone with Gnosis, regardless of whether they speak the same language. It can convey any nature of idea, even linguistic puns that only work in a single language by invoking the supernal truths and meanings behind those words to make anyone understand it implicitly. It is also even possible to convey untruths although any subterfuge rolls while speaking the High Speech suffer a -2 penalty as they language tries to convey symbols of untruth and deception that must be hidden. It feels noticeably different to the listener however and cannot be mistaken for regular High Speech.<br /> <br /> This form of High Speech cannot be used as a Yantra.<br /> <br /> +1 Reach - The spell allows extremely complex ideas to be woven into a single spoken word, an entire book could be summarized in a single page of High Speech text. A number of extended expression rolls equal to the spell's potency to convey a concept can be performed as an instant action but only to others who can understand High Speech. At the storyteller's discretion other skills may be appropriate instead such as science to explain a scientific concept.<br /> +2 Reach - The spell deceives the listener into believing that they're hearing regular High Speech by weaving a veiling effect into the spell. This can provoke a clash of wills against any spell to detect falsehoods.<br /> +2 Reach - The spell prevents the target from using regular High Speech, thus preventing its use as a spell Yantra. (This may sound unbalanced, but it's not really any different from paralyzing a person so they can't use a rote mudra or taking someone's voice so they can't use a mantra anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:35:44-07:00","id":950387,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in seeing how the Tamers of Air get updated to 2e, since they associate their Elemental Air with Truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T08:14:23-07:00","id":950559,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6748_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6748\" data-vbnamecard=\"6748\">Michael Kenner</a>, can I burrow Lost Words and Subtle Speech spells for the <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants\">High Speech Variants option topi</a></b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/900642-2e-option-high-speech-variants\"><b>c</b></a>? They seems as perfect for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum